From: Hampus Hellsberg <hampushellsberg@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] setup: make smpp.twisted3 an extra, only pySim-smpp2sim.py needs it

smpp.twisted3 is imported by pySim-smpp2sim.py alone; no module under
pySim/ uses it. Every release of smpp.twisted3 pins Twisted~=23.10.0,
a Twisted with three open advisories (CVE-2026-42304, CVE-2024-41810,
CVE-2024-41671), so every installation of the library carries a Twisted
it never loads and cannot upgrade. Move the requirement to a
`smpp2sim` extra; the script keeps working with `pip install
"pysim[smpp2sim]"` and fails with a plain ImportError without it, the
same way the `smdpp` extra behaves for klein.
---
 requirements.txt | 1 -
 setup.py         | 4 +++-
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/requirements.txt b/requirements.txt
--- a/requirements.txt
+++ b/requirements.txt
@@ -14,5 +14,4 @@
 git+https://github.com/osmocom/asn1tools
 packaging
 git+https://github.com/hologram-io/smpp.pdu
-smpp.twisted3 @ git+https://github.com/jookies/smpp.twisted
 smpplib
diff --git a/setup.py b/setup.py
--- a/setup.py
+++ b/setup.py
@@ -33,7 +33,6 @@ setup(
         "packaging",
         "smpp.pdu @ git+https://github.com/hologram-io/smpp.pdu",
         "asn1tools",
-        "smpp.twisted3 @ git+https://github.com/jookies/smpp.twisted",
     ],
     scripts=[
         'pySim-prog.py',
@@ -57,7 +56,10 @@ setup(
             "requests",
             "smpplib",
         ],
+        "smpp2sim": [
+            "smpp.twisted3 @ git+https://github.com/jookies/smpp.twisted",
+        ],
         "CardKeyProviderPgsql": [
             "psycopg2-binary",
         ]
